orum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T08:11:13-07:00","id":1393098,"title":"","content":"After having finally my translated Deluxe version I can say it is really good though it has two disadvantages.<br /> First is, it is not really makeing clear, who talks now in Beckett's notes and I feel like it is with his Medias in Res approach not really suitable for newcommers to learn the history. Maybe it will get better when I am able to work through all of the over 500 pages but with starting from page one feels confusing. It more feels like we stumbled apone his lost diary then his work to make newly embraced kindred the world easier. There I find the Prolog of Aristotle de Laurant's Book of Nod better because it is more clear how it get copied.<br /> <br /> Second there should be an explenation of who is who in his notes that should not need to be searched somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T13:30:02-07:00","id":1393841,"title":"","content":"It was a fantastic book. I enjoyed it hugely. The Brujah section was a